<title>USA: USDA offers Turkey credit guarantees on spirits.</title>
<headline>USDA offers Turkey credit guarantees on spirits.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Agriculture Department on Friday said it was offering export credit guarantees to Turkey to facilitate sales of grain neutral spirits.</p>
<p>The commodity was added to other goods eligible for the short-term GSM-102 credits. The USDA said the total available to Turkey in the credits remained at $180 million for fiscal 1997, which ends September 30.</p>
</text>
